-- title:
--   Reducing power series coefficients modulo a finitely generated ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $\sigma$ be a type of indeterminates, let $R$ be a commutative ring, and let $I$ be an ideal of $R$ which is finitely generated. Let $I\cdot R[[X_\sigma]]$ denote the image ideal `I.map (MvPowerSeries.C)`, i.e. the ideal of the multivariate formal power series ring $R[[X_\sigma]]$ generated by the constant series $C(r)$ for $r \in I$. The assertion is that there exists an isomorphism of $R$-algebras $$e : R[[X_\sigma]] \big/ I\cdot R[[X_\sigma]] \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; (R/I)[[X_\sigma]]$$ such that, for every $p \in R[[X_\sigma]]$, the value of $e$ on the class of $p$ modulo $I\cdot R[[X_\sigma]]$ is the coefficientwise reduction `MvPowerSeries.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) p`, the power series whose coefficient at each monomial $m$ is the class in $R/I$ of the coefficient of $m$ in $p$. Thus the isomorphism is not merely asserted abstractly but pinned down as the map induced by reduction of coefficients.
--
--   A piece of commutative algebra about formal power series rings: the extension of scalars $R[[X_\sigma]]/I\cdot R[[X_\sigma]] \cong (R/I)[[X_\sigma]]$, valid for finitely generated $I$. Finite generation is what forces a power series all of whose coefficients lie in $I$ to belong to the extended ideal. It is used to pass between power series over a coefficient ring and power series over a quotient of it, for instance over a residue field, and is cited by [`MvPowerSeries.exists_coords_of_quotient_span_finite_free`](thm.html#MvPowerSeries.exists_coords_of_quotient_span_finite_free).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_exists_algEquiv_quotient_map_C.lean

import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPowerSeries.Inverse
import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.Noetherian

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u v w

theorem MvPowerSeries.exists_algEquiv_quotient_map_C {σ : Type u} {R : Type v} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R) (hI : I.FG) : ∃ e : (MvPowerSeries σ R ⧸ I.map (MvPowerSeries.C (σ := σ) (R := R))) ≃ₐ[R] MvPowerSeries σ (R ⧸ I), ∀ p : MvPowerSeries σ R, e (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I.map (MvPowerSeries.C (σ := σ) (R := R))) p) = MvPowerSeries.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) p := by sorry
